<h2>Why does Pi lag behind Claude Code, Grok Build and Codex on plugins?</h2>
<p class="answer">Pi has no native plugin marketplace installer, so our harness installs each plugin's GitHub repository as a Pi package and checks whether Pi detects skills where it looks for them.</p>
[[SMX:PLUGIN_BY_AGENT_TABLE]]
<p>On [[SMX:LATEST_DATE_FMT]], Pi passed [[SMX:PI_PLUGIN_PASS]] of [[SMX:PI_PLUGIN_TOTAL]] tested plugins ([[SMX:PI_PLUGIN_RATE]]%). Compare that with our Nov 20, 2026 baseline (<code>testing/results/2026-11-20.json</code>), where Pi passed 55 of 86 plugins (64.0%) while Codex hit 65 of 65 (100%), Grok Build hit 326 of 332 (98.2%), and Claude Code hit 311 of 317 (98.1%). Most Pi failures are layout mismatches: the GitHub repository downloads cleanly, but its skills are packaged in another agent's directory convention rather than where Pi's <code>get_commands</code> RPC expects them.</p>

<h2>What got fixed, broke or turned flaky this week?</h2>
<p class="answer">Our scorecard separates real regressions from one-night network noise by requiring two consecutive failures to mark a tool broken.</p>
